Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. mjlab — Apache-2.0 (NOT MIT)
   https://github.com/mujocolab/mjlab
   Frozen at v1.6.0, commit 0fb8a681136be94ffc636a3dd423cabb97d91f10.
   License text: licenses/Apache-2.0.txt

   Used as the reference implementation for the Unitree G1 tracking evaluator
   in this repository. The following remain Apache-2.0 and are not relicensed by
   this repository:

   * assets/g1/g1.xml and assets/g1/assets/*.STL
     (G1 29-DoF MJCF and 35 mesh files, copied verbatim from mjlab's
     asset_zoo/robots/unitree_g1/xmls; 36 files, sha256
     ae606600e1089fe79412054852092673ebbef8df881caa9c3e291b8894b0396a)
   * the numerical constants transcribed into
     benchmark/evaluator/constants.py
     (reward scales, termination thresholds, actuator stiffness/damping
     derivation, observation layout, simulation options). Only the constants
     are derived from mjlab; the surrounding evaluator code is original and
     MIT-licensed.

   mjlab in turn redistributes the Unitree G1 robot description originating
   from Unitree Robotics; see mjlab's asset zoo for the upstream provenance.

2. LAFAN1 Retargeting Dataset — not redistributed
   lvhaidong/LAFAN1_Retargeting_Dataset (g1), revision
   07ff8845a94d59d4195a8ac04fe918d4e6338239.
   The 40 motion clips used by the benchmark are intentionally NOT part of this
   repository (data/ is gitignored). They are fetched by
   scripts/fetch_lafan1.py at the pinned revision.
   Please cite the dataset as described by its authors. The source motion capture
   data is from LAFAN1 (Holden, Kanoun, Pere, Komura, "Learned Motion Matching",
   ACM TOG / SIGGRAPH 2020).

